# Docker build context excludes.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs only `rust-toolchain.toml` from the build
# context (the real build runs via the `/workspace` bind mount in
# docker-compose, not a COPY of the source tree). So the purpose of
# this file is purely to keep the build *context transfer* small:
# without it, `docker build` ships the whole repo — including the
# ~12 GB `target/` and the `.git/` history — to the daemon on every
# invocation. The `book` stage does not COPY docs/ or crates/ either,
# so excluding build artifacts here cannot break any stage.

# --- Build artifacts (the big one: ~12 GB) ---------------------------
target/
**/target/

# --- VCS (Dockerfile never uses git; SHA tags come from CI metadata) -
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Language caches / deps (supplied at runtime via volumes/mounts) -
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Generated outputs (regenerated inside the container) ------------
**/dist/
crates/aozora-wasm/pkg/

# --- Editor / OS noise ----------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
